  "conceptId": "flu-hydrostatic-paradox",
  "type": "concept",
  "front": "A swimming pool and a drinking straw are filled with water to the same depth. Compare the pressure at the bottom of each, and the force on the bottom of each.",
  "back": "The pressures are equal. The forces are not: F = PA, and the pool's bottom has a far greater area, so the force on it is far greater."
