  "type": "choice",
  "front": "Does a hydraulic lift create energy?",
  "back": "No. Work out equals work in for an ideal fluid, and less than that for a real one with viscosity and seal friction. The claim that it creates energy would make a perpetual motion machine out of a jack and a bucket."
