  "conceptId": "flu-buoyancy",
  "type": "concept",
  "front": "Why is the buoyant force upward? Answer from pressure, not from Archimedes.",
  "back": "The bottom of a submerged object is deeper than the top, so the fluid pressure there is greater, so the upward push on the bottom exceeds the downward push on the top. The side forces cancel in pairs. What is left is a net upward force."
