  "modelAnswer": "The sign of the acceleration says which way the acceleration points, not whether the speed is increasing. Whether an object speeds up or slows down is decided by comparing the signs of velocity and acceleration: same signs means speeding up, opposite signs means slowing down. An object travelling in the negative direction with a positive acceleration is therefore slowing down — the acceleration opposes the motion. The student's rule happens to be right whenever the velocity is positive, which is why it survives, but it fails on every negative velocity.",
