  "modelAnswer": "Second-phase acceleration is the slope of the velocity graph: $\\frac{-2.0 - 6.0}{8.0 - 4.0} = -2.0$ m/s$^2$. The graph crosses zero when $6.0 - 2.0(t - 4.0) = 0$, at $t = 7.0$ s. Areas: rectangle $(6.0)(4.0) = +24$ m; triangle from 4.0 to 7.0 s, $\\frac{1}{2}(3.0)(6.0) = +9.0$ m; triangle from 7.0 to 8.0 s, $\\frac{1}{2}(1.0)(2.0) = 2.0$ m in size but below the axis, so $-2.0$ m. Displacement $= 24 + 9.0 - 2.0 = +31$ m. Distance $= 24 + 9.0 + 1.0 = 34$ m.",
