  "modelAnswer": "(a) $I = (1.5)(0.20)^2 + (1.5)(0.40)^2 + (1.5)(0.60)^2 = 0.060 + 0.240 + 0.540 = 0.84$ kg$\\cdot$m$^2$. (b) $\\alpha = \\tau_{\\mathrm{net}}/I = 2.1/0.84 = 2.5$ rad/s$^2$. (c) All three at 0.40 m gives $I = 3(1.5)(0.40)^2 = 0.72$ kg$\\cdot$m$^2$, which is smaller, so $\\alpha = 2.1/0.72 = 2.9$ rad/s$^2$ — larger, by a factor of $0.84/0.72 = 1.17$. Same total mass, different distribution, different response to the same torque.",
