  "prompt": "Water (density 1000 kg/m³) flows steadily through a horizontal pipe. In the wide section the radius is 0.060 m and the speed is 1.2 m/s; the absolute pressure there is 2.00 x 10^5 Pa. The pipe narrows to a radius of 0.030 m. Take g = 9.8 m/s². (a) Find the speed in the narrow section. (b) Find the volume flow rate. (c) Find the absolute pressure in the narrow section.",
  "modelAnswer": "(a) Continuity: A_1 v_1 = A_2 v_2 with A proportional to r². The radius halves, so the area is one quarter and v_2 = 4 x 1.2 = 4.8 m/s.\n\n(b) A_1 = pi(0.060)² = 1.13 x 10^-2 m². Volume flow rate = A_1 v_1 = 1.13 x 10^-2 x 1.2 = 1.4 x 10^-2 m³/s.\n\n(c) The pipe is horizontal so the rho g y terms are equal and cancel. Bernoulli gives P_2 = P_1 + (1/2) rho (v_1² - v_2²) = 2.00 x 10^5 + 500 x (1.44 - 23.04) = 2.00 x 10^5 - 1.08 x 10^4 = 1.89 x 10^5 Pa.",
