          "for": "Identifies a specific source of uncertainty and states its effect — for example, human reaction time at the start and stop of the timing, which shifts every measured total time and is reduced but not eliminated by timing 20 oscillations; or measuring the pendulum length to the top of the bob rather than to its centre of mass, which makes every length systematically too short."
